For $x=\mu=\sigma=1$, the formula gives $e^{-2}\approx0.1353353$; the finite-$L$ exit probabilities were computed and shown to approach that value. The proof uses the standard bounded-stopping theorem with its boundedness and almost-sure exit conditions made explicit. No model-specific control law or almost-sure default assertion is established. The original duplicate/unrecoverable classification and source ID remain unchanged.

